Yaoning Chen is currently a professor at the College of Environmental Science and Engineering of Hunan University. He obtained his Bachelor’s degree in biochemical engineering from Beijing Institute of Technology in 2000. And he earned his Ph.D. degree in environmental engineering education at the College of Environmental Science and Engineering, Hunan University in 2007. His current research interests include organic solid waste treatment, resource utilization, and advanced oxidation process.
Huayue Kang received his Bachelor’s degree in 2022 at Nanchang Hangkong University, China. At present, he is currently pursuing his Master’s degree under the supervision of Prof. Yaoning Chen at the College of Environmental Science and Engineering, Hunan University. His research interests mainly focus on MOF-based carbon materials for application in advanced oxidation processes.
Min Cheng received his Ph.D. degree under the supervision of Prof. Guangming Zeng from Hunan University, China, in 2018. He is currently an associate professor at the College of Environmental Science and Engineering, Hunan University. His current research interests focus on the development of MOF-based materials and porous materials for applications in catalysis and separation.
